+1. [x] **No visible windows.** Every optimizer process is spawned with `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` on Windows (`crates/ta-daemon/src/prompt_optimizer_supervisor.rs` currently sets no flag and the constant appears nowhere in the repo). A test asserts the flag on the constructed command; a manual Windows smoke check is added to the release checklist.
+2. [x] **Flap guard.** After the existing five failures in five minutes the optimizer is disabled for the session with one user-visible message, never restarted forever; `ta compression status` shows restart count and last failure.
+3. [x] **`ta-context-opt` crate.** Traits `InputOptimizer`, `ContextOptimizer`, `OutputOptimizer`; a registry selected per slot in config; a `none` implementation; and a metrics record `{bytes_in, bytes_out, est_tokens_in, est_tokens_out, ms, lossless, original_ref}` with the full original kept on disk so any reduction is reversible. `[compression.plugin]` becomes the `proxy` kind of the input slot.
+4. [x] **Replay-able selection.** `--set optimizers.input.use=none|rtk|headroom` works through `ta golden replay`.
+5. [x] Tests and docs: slot selection, `none` baseline, metrics and original recovery, spawn flag. `docs/USAGE.md` how-to including licences recorded per optimizer.
+
+**Notes (implementation)**: `build_command` in `prompt_optimizer_supervisor.rs` is the single place optimizer processes are built; the flag is asserted on its returned `creation_flags` because `tokio::process::Command` has no getter, and it is only passed to the OS under `cfg(windows)`, so the manual Windows smoke check is in `docs/RELEASING.md`. The flap guard keeps the existing suspend-and-wait-for-`ta compression enable` mechanism and adds the single user-visible message plus `last_failure` and `last_failure_at` in status. Selection is resolved by `ta_context_opt::resolve_selection` in `ta run` (`compression_base_url`); `optimizers.input.use=none` routes nothing, naming a proxy the daemon is not supervising refuses the launch. The `context` and `output` slots have traits, registry and `none` but no shipped non-`none` implementation. The `headroom` and `rtk` licences are recorded as unverified and need confirming upstream.
