-ta compression enable   # clears suspended state; supervisor retries within 5 s
+ta compression enable   # clears the disabled state; supervisor retries within 5 s
+
+### Optimizer slots
+
+Input, context and output optimization are three slots. Each slot names one optimizer, so an open-source tool can be started with and swapped later without code changes.
+
+```toml
+# .ta/daemon.toml
+[optimizers.input]
+use = "headroom"   # none | headroom | rtk | the name of your [compression.plugin]
+
+[optimizers.context]
+use = "none"
+
+[optimizers.output]
+use = "none"
+```
+
+- Leave a slot out to keep today's behaviour: the input slot is the `[compression]` proxy, the others are `none`.
+- `none` is the baseline. With `use = "none"` on the input slot no proxy is started and agents call the API directly.
+- `[compression.plugin]` is the `proxy` kind of the input slot. Its `name` is what you put in `use`.
+- `ta compression status` lists each slot with its optimizer, kind and licence.
+- Licences are recorded per optimizer. `none` is built in. For `headroom` and `rtk` the licence is shown as unverified until it has been confirmed upstream, so check it before bundling either.
+
+An unknown name fails with the list of valid names rather than silently running the baseline.
+
+**Compare optimizers on identical work.** The slot is replayable through the golden set:
+
+```bash
+ta golden replay <entry> --set optimizers.input.use=none --tag no-optimizer
+ta golden replay <entry> --set optimizers.input.use=headroom --tag headroom
+ta golden report <entry>
+```
+
+The daemon supervises one input proxy at a time. Replaying with a proxy other than the supervised one stops the launch with the steps to switch (`[compression.plugin] name = ...`, then `ta daemon restart`), because running the baseline instead would make the comparison meaningless.
+
+**Reversible reductions.** The `ta-context-opt` library keeps the full original on disk (`<sha256>.orig`) for any reduction and records `bytes_in`, `bytes_out`, estimated tokens in and out, `ms`, `lossless` and an `original_ref` that recovers it. A reduction is never applied if its original cannot be saved.
